6. VS Code Integration Requirements


6.1 MCP Server
System shall expose a local MCP (Model Context Protocol) server consumable by Copilot Agent Mode
MCP server shall expose tools: scan_project, ingest_framework, load_lld, run_conformance_check, get_deviation_report, explain_deviation, suggest_fix
MCP server shall be startable from VS Code command palette or automatically on workspace open
MCP server shall run as a local Node.js or Python process with no external network dependencies except Claude API

6.2 VS Code Extension
Extension shall provide a dedicated ArchGuard AI sidebar panel with architecture diagram viewer
Extension shall render C4 and PlantUML diagrams inside VS Code without external browser
Extension shall integrate with VS Code Problems panel to surface deviations as diagnostics
Extension shall support click-to-navigate from deviation to offending source line
Extension shall provide command palette entries for all major operations
Extension shall support on-save lightweight analysis with configurable scope

6.3 Copilot Agent Mode Integration
All analysis capabilities shall be accessible via natural language through Copilot Chat in Agent Mode
Agent Mode shall support queries such as: 'Has the payment module deviated from the LLD?', 'Show me all layer violations', 'What design patterns are incorrectly implemented?'
Agent Mode shall be able to explain any deviation in context of the specific code file open in the editor
Agent Mode shall suggest code fixes inline using VS Code editor integration

